// ============================================================================
//  mod_whoswho.zone  -  the five assets Who's Who's DOWNED-STATE OVERLAY needs,
//                       none of which ship outside Die Rise.
//
//  User, 2026-08-16: "the visual effect overlay screen effect was working at
//  some point in the mod's development but recently stopped working correctly,
//  the audio fx are still working after going down in who's who though ... all
//  you gotta do is make sure the currently missing overlay fx while downed in
//  the who's who perk state are there and not missing."
//
//  🌟 THE AUDIO WORKING IS WHAT NAILED THIS DOWN, AND IT RULED OUT EVERY SCRIPT
//  THEORY IN ONE STEP. Stock's _zm_chugabud::activate_chugabud_effects_and_audio()
//  (:745-762) writes BOTH clientfields from the same four lines:
//
//        maps\mp\_visionset_mgr::vsmgr_activate( "visionset", "zm_whos_who", self );
//        self setclientfieldtoplayer( "clientfield_whos_who_audio",  1 );
//        self setclientfieldtoplayer( "clientfield_whos_who_filter", 1 );
//
//  If the sting and the looper are audible then that function ran, the gate
//  level.whos_who_client_setup was set, create_corpse was 1, and the filter
//  clientfield was written in the same breath. So the script half is CORRECT and
//  has been all along - what is missing is on the other side of the callback.
//
//  🛑 THE OVERLAY IS TWO SEPARATE EFFECTS AND BOTH OF THEM NEED A DIE RISE ASSET:
//
//    1. the screen FILTER - zm_expanded.csc::zmqol_whoswho_filter() calls
//       _zm_perks::enable_filter_afterlife( player, 5 ), which hands filter pass
//       5 the material `generic_filter_afterlife`.
//    2. the COLOUR GRADE - _visionset_mgr applies the visionset named
//       "zm_whos_who", which is the rawfile vision/zm_whos_who.vision.
//
//  Measured across an index of all 191 fastfiles in zone\all plus zone\english,
//  generated with Unlinker --list. Every one of these appears in EXACTLY ONE
//  fastfile, zm_highrise.ff:
//
//      zm_highrise.txt:3953   rawfile,     vision/zm_whos_who.vision
//      zm_highrise.txt:7445   techniqueset,sw4_2d_afterlife_q51e4w21
//      zm_highrise.txt:7446   image,       zm_whoswho_warpblur
//      zm_highrise.txt:7447   image,       zm_whoswho_mask
//      zm_highrise.txt:7448   material,    generic_filter_afterlife
//
//  So on TranZit / Diner / Nuketown / Origins the client asked for a material
//  and a visionset that are not loaded. Neither of those is an error in T6 - the
//  filter pass draws nothing and the visionset is a no-op - which is exactly the
//  reported symptom: audio yes, picture no.
//
//  📝 "It worked at some point" is true and consistent: zmqol_whoswho_enabled()
//  returns 0 on zm_highrise because that map ships the perk itself, so on Die
//  Rise the overlay has always come from stock with all five assets present.
//  Every other map has never had them.
//
//  🛑 NO NEW --load IS NEEDED. build_ff.bat already loads zm_highrise.ff (line
//  332), and it sits AFTER the zombies commons, so first-load-wins keeps every
//  shared asset name on its zombies copy. Nothing about the load order changes.
//
//  📝 THE TECHSET IS DELIBERATELY NOT LISTED. The Linker resolves a material's
//  techniqueset transitively out of the loaded donor; the built mod.ff is
//  checked for sw4_2d_afterlife_q51e4w21 after every link rather than trusting
//  that. If it is ever absent, add it here.
//
//  📝 THE TWO IMAGES CARRY THEIR OWN PIXELS. A T6 fastfile stores only an image
//  HEADER - the pixels come from a loose .iwi - so both were rebuilt from the
//  Treyarch source PNGs in the workspace
//  (BlackOps3Shaders\source_data\shader_templates\_images\, which is where the
//  BO2-era zm_whoswho_* sources live) through png2dds.ps1 -> ImageConverter,
//  and land in zone_assets\images\ so build.bat packs them into mod.iwd.
//  Dimensions cross-checked against the real BO2 payload: the dlczm1 IPAK dump's
//  zm_whoswho_mask.dds is 32,896 bytes = 256x256 DXT1 + header, and the PNG is
//  256x256. Same asset.
// ============================================================================

image,zm_whoswho_warpblur
image,zm_whoswho_mask

material,generic_filter_afterlife

rawfile,vision/zm_whos_who.vision

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  v1.99.17 - THE FOUR GLOW-CAPABLE CLONE MODELS.
//
//  The Who's Who corpse glows because the model it is built from uses the `_g`
//  material variants, which are authored to read the shader constant stock
//  writes (`scriptVector3`). Read straight out of the dumped GLBs:
//
//    c_zom_player_reporter_dlc1_fb (Die Rise) -> mtl_..._arm_g / _body_g /
//                                                _gear_g / _head_g
//    c_zom_player_reporter_fb      (TranZit)  -> mtl_..._arm / _body /
//                                                _gear / _head
//
//  🛑 Every `mc/mtl_c_zom_player_*_g` material in the game lives in
//  zm_highrise.ff and nowhere else, so off Die Rise the clone is made of
//  materials that cannot glow and the shader constant lands on nothing.
//
//  Declaring the four models brings their `_g` materials and images with them
//  transitively. zm_highrise.ff is already in build_ff.bat's --load list, so no
//  load-order change.
//
//  📝 Only the Victis four exist. The Nuketown agents and the Origins crew have
//  no `_g` materials anywhere in the game, which is why
//  zmqol_whoswho_glow_model_watch() is gated to zm_transit.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
xmodel,c_zom_player_oldman_dlc1_fb
xmodel,c_zom_player_reporter_dlc1_fb
xmodel,c_zom_player_farmgirl_dlc1_fb
xmodel,c_zom_player_engineer_dlc1_fb
